{
  "tema": 6234,
  "slug": "todo-pronombre",
  "titulo": "Todo = everything, todos = everyone",
  "subtitulo": "Todo está listo. Todos quieren surfear.",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "Alone, todo means everything (singular verb) and todos/todas means everyone or all of them (plural verb). When todo refers to something already mentioned, it agrees with it and usually goes with an object pronoun: me las comí todas.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Todo** on its own = _everything_. It takes a **singular** verb: **Todo está listo.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Todos** = _everyone, all of them_ (**todas** if they're all female). It takes a **plural** verb: **Todos saben.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "When it refers to something already mentioned, **todo** agrees with it: **todo, toda, todos, todas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "As the object, it usually comes with **lo, la, los, las**: **¿Y las tortillas? —Me las comí todas.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "(lo / la / los / las)",
            "+ verb +",
            "todo / toda / todos / todas"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Todo el mundo** = _everyone_, but with a **singular** verb: **Todo el mundo sabe.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **todo** is the whole pot; **todos** are the people around it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
